      "content": "Sure, I'd be happy to help! Voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives differ in terms of vocal cord activity. For /z/, the alveolar fricative, the vocal cords vibrate while air passes through the narrow gap between the tongue and the alveolar ridge, producing a buzzing sound. In contrast, for /s/, the unvoiced alveolar fricative, the vocal cords don't vibrate; the sound is created by the hissing effect of air passing through the same gap without vocal cord involvement.",
